Description: black hole widget for the terminal
 eventhorizon draws Jean-Pierre Luminet's 1979 plot of a black hole live in
 the terminal: a thin accretion disk around a Schwarzschild black hole, with
 its light bent by gravity, turning at true Keplerian rates so the picture
 never repeats.
 .
 In terminals that support the kitty graphics protocol, such as kitty and
 Ghostty, it draws in real pixels; elsewhere it uses braille dots. It has
 presets, a status line, events such as a probe falling in and a cuneiform
 transmission, and lowers its frame rate when its window loses focus.
 .
 It is built on luminet, a Python library for simulating Schwarzschild black
 holes, which is included along with its luminet command.
